## Expected Answer
Strong candidates discuss: 1) Unit tests for individual components (producers, consumers, brokers), 2) Integration tests for cluster coordination and leader election, 3) Chaos engineering testing network partitions and broker failures, 4) Mutation testing to verify test suite quality, 5) Property-based testing for message ordering guarantees.

## Code Example
```typescript
// Property-based test for message ordering
describe('Message Ordering Guarantees', () => {
  it('should maintain ordering within partitions', async () => {
    const testMessages = generateRandomMessages(1000);
    const partitionKey = 'test-key';

    // Send messages in known order
    for (const msg of testMessages) {
      await producer.send({ topic: 'test', key: partitionKey, value: msg });
    }

    // Verify consumer receives in same order
    const received = await consumer.consume({ topic: 'test', partition: 0 });
    expect(received.map(m => m.value)).toEqual(testMessages);
  });
});

// Mutation test example
describe('Broker Fault Tolerance', () => {
  it('should handle leader election during partition failure', async () => {
    // Simulate broker failure
    await chaosEngine.killBroker(leaderBrokerId);

    // Verify new leader is elected
    const newLeader = await cluster.getLeaderForPartition(partition);
    expect(newLeader).not.toBe(leaderBrokerId);

    // Verify no message loss during failover
    const beforeFailure = await getOffset(partition);
    const afterFailure = await getOffset(partition);
    expect(afterFailure).toBeGreaterThanOrEqual(beforeFailure);
  });
});
```

